# ADR Reporting & Documentation

## Project Overview

This simulated pharmacovigilance project demonstrates the structured documentation of an Adverse Drug Reaction (ADR) based on a patient case scenario.

The exercise focuses on identifying and documenting key information required for an individual case safety report (ICSR), including patient details, reporter information, suspected medicinal product, adverse event, seriousness, outcome, and relevant clinical information.

> **Disclaimer:** This is a simulated educational case created for pharmacovigilance training and portfolio purposes. It does not contain real patient data and is not an actual safety report.

