# 10. Case Narrative

A 52-year-old female patient with rheumatoid arthritis was receiving oral methotrexate 10 mg once weekly along with folic acid supplementation. During treatment, the patient developed mouth ulcers. The event was reported by a healthcare professional as a spontaneous initial report from India. The exact dates of treatment initiation and adverse event onset were not available. Dechallenge and rechallenge information were not reported. Based on the available information, methotrexate was identified as the suspected medicinal product.

