# 12. Documentation Principles Demonstrated

This exercise demonstrates the following pharmacovigilance documentation principles:

- Accurate recording of patient information
- Identification of the reporter
- Documentation of suspected medicinal product
- Documentation of concomitant medication
- Recording of adverse event information
- Assessment of seriousness criteria
- Documentation of treatment and event timelines
- Recording of dechallenge and rechallenge information
- Documentation of clinical narrative
- Identification of missing information
- Avoidance of unsupported assumptions

